WHY THIS AND NOT AN OPEN-SOURCE LICENCE

Recorded as decision D-AUDIT-4 in `docs/initial/decisions.md` (R-25), answering
audit finding #19 (`docs/progress/audit/2026-08-17.md`): the repository had no
LICENSE file at all, which means default copyright applied and nobody —
including a future collaborator or contractor — had any recorded grant.

This notice matches the actual distribution posture: Respin is a hosted
subscription product, not a distributable library, and no part of this
repository is published to a package registry. An OSI licence was deliberately
NOT adopted, because adopting one by default would be a real grant of rights
made by assumption rather than by choice.

SCOPE

This notice covers this repository's own source. It makes no claim about the
third-party dependencies vendored or referenced by it — `respin/pnpm-lock.yaml`,
`uv.lock`, and the NuGet package graph each carry their own licences, which are
their own.

This is a checklist posture recorded so the question has an answer. It is NOT
legal advice.
